[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am no longer seeing completions for private definitions in module 'A' while in module 'B' which has 'import all A'.</p>\n<p>Steps to reproduce. </p>\n<p>Foo/Bar.lean</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">privBar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"hello\"</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pubBar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"hello\"</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">end</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Foo/Baz.lean</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">baz</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I only see <code>pubBar</code> as an available completion after <code>Bar.</code> </p>\n<p>Platform/lean version:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">4.28</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">rc1</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Target</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x86_64</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">unknown</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">linux</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">gnu</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Minimal neovim config to reproduce (minimal, so not including cmp/blink. just using manual completions via C-x C-o).</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lua\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">vim</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"py\">opt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"py\">signcolumn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"yes:1\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Bootstrap lazy.nvim</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">local</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">lazypath</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"/tmp/completion_test/lazy.nvim\"</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ow\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">vim</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"py\">uv</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">fs_stat</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nv\">lazypath</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">then</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nv\">vim</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"py\">fn</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nf\">system</span><span class=\"p\">({</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">\"git\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">\"clone\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">\"--filter=blob:none\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">\"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"s2\">\"--branch=stable\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"nv\">lazypath</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n<span class=\"kr\">end</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">vim</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"py\">opt</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"py\">rtp</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"nf\">prepend</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nv\">lazypath</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"nb\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"lazy\"</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nf\">setup</span><span class=\"p\">({</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">\"Julian/lean.nvim\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">\"neovim/nvim-lspconfig\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"p\">},</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nv\">root</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"/tmp/completion_test\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">})</span>\n\n<span class=\"nb\">require</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">\"lean\"</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nf\">setup</span><span class=\"p\">()</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 577620035,
        "sender_full_name": "cmlsharp",
        "timestamp": 1772754875
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Without having looked too deeply, considering <code>Bar.privBar</code> works I can imagine there's an issue here, but the same issue appears reproducible in VSCode:</p>\n<p><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/ak1HV2duswVlvHAGNV2zi3t-/Screenshot-2026-03-05-at-19.05.13.png\">Screenshot 2026-03-05 at 19.05.13.png</a></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/ak1HV2duswVlvHAGNV2zi3t-/Screenshot-2026-03-05-at-19.05.13.png\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-03-05 at 19.05.13.png\"><img data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"864x367\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/ak1HV2duswVlvHAGNV2zi3t-/Screenshot-2026-03-05-at-19.05.13.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div><p>Which would point to this behavior being server-side.</p>",
        "id": 577621426,
        "sender_full_name": "Julian Berman",
        "timestamp": 1772755585
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(In my case that's 4.29.0-rc5 which it's always good to try, in theory we should check HEAD as well now.)</p>",
